xnu 0465: route the wlan sid around the smmu, and time the reason write

Two questions from the 2026-11-26 measurements.

The PBL consumes the doorbell, reads inside the 512 KiB it is told about and yet
never acks, at 4 KiB, 64 KiB or 512 KiB, with max read request size 128 or 512.
Every host register matches the donor's working boot, so the last unverified
link is the stage-2 table itself: this SoC reports no ATS, so W2 could never
prove a translation and a table pointing at the wrong pages would read garbage
without a fault. mondrianwifibypass=1 switches this SID to bypass and rings a
64 KiB copy of the image from the ABL's contiguous framebuffer at 0xb8000000: an
ack here and silence through translation names the table.

Separately, the reset without the wifi driver reaches fastboot and spends 2000 ms
in the PMIC restart reason, while with the wifi driver it does not finish inside
the 5 s the worker allows. mondrianreasonms=<ms> makes that bound a boot argument
so the real cost can be measured instead of guessed.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
index 2cf4945..2c415c0 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
@@ -1710,9 +1710,22 @@ mondrian_reset_to_bootloader(int recovery)
 		 * boots in a row). Five seconds still cannot strand the port,
 		 * and the elapsed time names the real cost.
 		 */
-		for (i = 0; i < 5000 && !mondrian_reason_done; i++) {
-			delay(1000);
-			waited = i;
+		{
+			int ms = 0;
+
+			/*
+			 * Measured 2026-11-26: 2000 ms without the wifi driver and more
+			 * than 5000 ms with it, so the wait is a boot argument while the
+			 * cost is being found.
+			 */
+			if (!PE_parse_boot_argn("mondrianreasonms", &ms, sizeof(ms)) ||
+			    ms < 100 || ms > 60000) {
+				ms = 5000;
+			}
+			for (i = 0; i < ms && !mondrian_reason_done; i++) {
+				delay(1000);
+				waited = i;
+			}
 		}
 		wrote = mondrian_reason_done;
 	}
